A search cancelled while it waits for a worker must not run: calculate() reset cancelRequested to false on entry, so a cancel that arrived first was lost and the search ran to its timeout for a bot that no longer wanted it (with a bounded, queueing executor that wait is real). A search cannot be reused, so the reset served nothing. The flag is also written by the server thread and read in the search's inner loop, so it is volatile.

